# Read by BuildKit as `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`, which takes precedence over a `.dockerignore` at
# the root of the build context. The build context here is the repository root (`context: ../..` in
# docker-compose.yml), which is why this file is named after the Dockerfile instead of being a plain
# `.dockerignore` — a plain one at this path is never read.
#
# Patterns without a slash only match at the context root, so anything nested needs `**/`.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/rush-logs
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.env*
# Rush's workspace temp dir holds the pnpm store: about 967MB on this machine, and rebuilt inside the
# image from the lockfile anyway.
common/temp
# The host side of the compose log bind mount.
**/logs
# The image build only needs to produce dist/. `test/**` is still typechecked by `rushx typecheck` on
# the host; drop this line if you would rather have the container's `tsc --noEmit` cover it too.
**/test
